                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h2][b]7/10[/b][/h2] – Tommy guns, trench coats, gangsters, and enough slow-motion gunfights to make my inner 12-year-old very happy. Chicago 1930 feels like a dusty time capsule from the era when games were rough around the edges but had buckets of personality. The controls may show their age, but the nostalgia hits harder than a Tommy gun. 🔫🍸🕴️\r\n\r\nFollow for vintage shootouts, questionable mob decisions, and games that smell like old PC boxes. 🕴️💰🎮 [b]https://store.steampowered.com/curator/42602807-Osiris-Reviews/[/b]",
